 "coverage": "99 ICs and 329 nets over 1284 pins, from DICE's netlist of the game. DICE is an emulator: its netlist is the circuit as it simulates it, at the board positions the drawings use, and is not a drawing of the board. Where it stands an RC delay or a speed hack in a wire, the wire is restored; what it models that is not a chip on the board (3OR, CLOCK_14_318_MHZ, COIN_INPUT, DIPSWITCH, JOYSTICK1_INPUT, LATCH, START_INPUT) is left off the board view, and the resistors and capacitors are not named at all. Supply pins are joined to +5V and GND from each part's pinout. The ICs sit at their board positions, on the grid spacing of Atari's boards.",
